{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_FrTSyn_00019","versions":[{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_FrTSyn_00019","release":"R19-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_FrTSyn_00019","release":"R20-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_FrTSyn_00019@rel:R21-11#afa5593c","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_FrTSyn_00019","release":"R21-11","content":"For each configured Time Master (refer to FrTSynGlobal- TimeMaster ) the FrTSyn module shall periodically transmit SYNC messages with the cycle FrTSynGlobalTimeTxPeriod including the time value, which will be valid at the start of the next FlexRay cycle 0 and User Data, if the GLOBAL_TIME_BASE bit within the timeBaseStatus is set and FrTSynGlobalTimeTxPeriod is unequal to 0 and if the associated cyclicMsgResumeCounter is not running. The cyclic transmission shall be started in the earliest possible FrT- Syn_MainFunction call once the requirements above are fulfilled.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_TimeSyncOverFlexRay.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:13:07+00:00","cleaning":{"rule":"spec-text-clean@1","raw_sha256":"afa5593c42e7a0cab81c754a0ff008187f062acf75e403e0770263a7239ece4a","removed":["24 of 71 Document ID 675: AUTOSAR_SWS_TimeSyncOverFlexRay Specification of Time Synchronization over FlexRay AUTOSAR CP R21-11"]},"text_key":"9dcaff1642dd"},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_FrTSyn_00019","release":"R22-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_FrTSyn_00019","release":"R23-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_FrTSyn_00019","release":"R24-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf